# MP3 Cutter API configuration.
#
# config.py reads these via pydantic-settings, from the real environment first and
# then from a .env file sitting next to it. Field names map to upper-case env
# vars, so `allowed_origins` is set with ALLOWED_ORIGINS.
#
#   cp .env.example .env


# ─── ALLOWED_ORIGINS — the one you must set ──────────────────────────────────
#
# Comma-separated list of browser origins permitted to call this API. It becomes
# CORSMiddleware's allow_origins in main.py.
#
# If the calling site is not in this list, Starlette sends NO
# Access-Control-Allow-Origin header at all, and the browser blocks the response
# with:
#
#   Access to fetch at 'https://api.example.com/api/cut' from origin
#   'https://example.com' has been blocked by CORS policy: No
#   'Access-Control-Allow-Origin' header is present on the requested resource.
#
# The request itself succeeds — you will see 200 in the server log — so this looks
# like a network fault from the front end when it is purely a configuration one.
#
# Matching is exact on scheme, host and port. Consequences worth knowing:
#   - http:// and https:// are different origins.
#   - www and non-www are different origins. List both if both resolve.
#   - NO trailing slash. "https://example.com/" will not match.
#   - Preview and staging domains each need their own entry.
#
# Production:
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://mp3cutteronline.com,https://www.mp3cutteronline.com
#
# Local development against the Astro dev server (port 4321) or the old Next.js
# one (3000):
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:4321,http://localhost:3000


# ─── Everything below is optional; these are the defaults ────────────────────

# Absolute path to the ffmpeg binary. Leave as-is if it is on PATH.
# FFMPEG_PATH=ffmpeg

# Upload cap, in megabytes. Enforced twice: once against Content-Length before
# python-multipart buffers anything, and again while streaming to disk.
# MAX_FILE_SIZE_MB=500

# Sliding-window rate limit, per client. Every endpoint spawns ffmpeg and holds a
# decoded copy of the audio in memory, so an unauthenticated caller can exhaust
# the host without these.
# RATE_LIMIT_REQUESTS=20
# RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW_SECONDS=60

# Ceiling on files /split may emit, and the shortest segment it will cut. Without
# these a request for a million segments turns a small upload into a zip bomb.
# MAX_SPLIT_SEGMENTS=500
# MIN_SEGMENT_DURATION_SECONDS=0.5

# Longest ringtone /ringtone will produce, in seconds.
# MAX_RINGTONE_SECONDS=40

# Scratch directory for in-flight uploads. Each request gets an isolated
# subdirectory that is deleted as soon as the response body has been flushed.
# TEMP_DIR=/tmp/mp3cutter
